<setup>
  <selectFromSequence name="k" from="2" to="4" step="1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="b" from="-5" to="5" step="1" exclude="$k -$k -1 0 1 $a -$a"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="a" from="2" to="4" step="1" exclude="$k"/>
  <function name="c" variable="n">(-1)^(n-1)*(n-1)!/$k^n</function>
  
  <function name="f">cos(x)</function>
  <derivative name="fP">$f</derivative>
  <derivative name="fPP">$fP</derivative>
  <derivative name="fPPP">$fPP</derivative>
  <derivative name="fP4">$fPPP</derivative>

  <function name="genTerm" variables="x n">$k*(-1)^n/$a^n*(x-$a)^n</function>
</setup>
<p>
  Consider a function <m>f</m> for which the following information is known:
</p>

      <p>
        <tabular>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f($a) = $b</m></cell>
                  <cell><m>f'($a) = \frac{1}{$k}</m></cell>
                  <cell><m>f''($a) = $$c(2)</m></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell><m>f'''($a) = $$c(3)</m></cell>
                  <cell><m>f^{(4)}($a) = $$c(4)</m></cell>
                  <cell><m>f^{(5)}($a) = $$c(5)</m></cell>
                </row>
              </tabular>
      </p>

      <p>
        State the first 6 terms of the Taylor series of <m>f</m> centered at <m>a = $a</m> by completing the blanks below; note that there is one blank per term and that several of the terms involve the variable <m>x</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <m>T_f(x) = </m><answer>$b</answer><m>+</m><answer>1/$k*(x-$a)</answer><m>+</m><answer>$$c(2)/2! * (x-$a)^2</answer><m>+</m><answer>$$c(3)/3! * (x-$a)^3</answer><m>+</m><answer>$$c(4)/4! * (x-$a)^4</answer><m>+</m><answer>$$c(5)/5! * (x-$a)^5</answer><m>+ \cdots</m>
      </p>
